---
title: Greek Salad
servings: 4
cuisine: greek
main_protein: dairy
prep_time: "15 minutes"
cook_time: "0 minutes"
tags:
  - side
image: ../obsidian/attachments/IMG_6374.jpeg
prep:
  - Mince 1 garlic clove
  - Halve, seed and slice the cucumber 0.25 inch thick
  - Halve 2 cups cherry tomatoes
  - Cube the feta and thinly slice the red onion
---

Make the dressing. In a #small bowl{}, whisk together the @extra virgin olive oil{0.25%cup}, @red wine vinegar{1%tablespoon} (or normal vinegar), @garlic{1%clove}, minced, @dried oregano{0.5%teaspoon}, @dijon mustard{0.25%teaspoon}, @sea salt{0.25%teaspoon} and freshly ground @black pepper{}.

Make the salad. In a #large bowl{}, combine the @english cucumber{1}, cut lengthwise, seeded, and sliced 0.25-inch thick, @cherry tomatoes{2%cups}, halved, @feta cheese{5%ounces}, cut into 0.5-inch cubes, and @red onion{0.33%cup}, thinly sliced.

Pour the dressing over the salad and toss to combine. Sprinkle with more dried oregano and serve.

